From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ROCKNIX <rocknix@rocknix.org>
Date: Mon, 17 Mar 2026 23:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] miyoo-serial: improved joystick with frame sync, EMA
 smoothing, miyoo-* DTS properties

Major improvements to the Miyoo serial joystick path:

1. Byte-by-byte frame synchronisation (miyoo_read_frame):
   Auto-recovers from UART desync instead of permanently misaligning
   on partial reads.

2. Exponential Moving Average (EMA) smoothing:
   The Miyoo MCU sends axis data as single bytes (0-255), giving only
   ~115 usable steps per axis.  A configurable EMA (miyoo-smoothing
   DTS property, 0-256, default 160) smooths calibrated values before
   deadzone processing.

3. VMIN=0 / VTIME=1 for non-blocking TTY reads:
   Allows kthread_should_stop() and the inactivity timer to be checked
   periodically, enabling clean shutdown and reliable recovery.

4. Miyoo-specific DTS properties (miyoo-deadzone, miyoo-fuzz,
   miyoo-flat, miyoo-{lx,ly,rx,ry}-{p,n}-tuning, miyoo-smoothing)
   instead of reusing the shared button-adc-* / abs_*-tuning names.

5. Calibration frames increased from 50 to 100 for a more accurate
   zero-point determination.

6. Removed the static float miyoo_deadzone_ratio.

DTS properties (Miyoo serial path):
  miyoo-deadzone    absolute deadzone in [-32760..32760] range
  miyoo-fuzz        input fuzz for ABS params
  miyoo-flat        input flat for ABS params
  miyoo-smoothing   EMA alpha 0-256 (256 = off, default 160)
  miyoo-{lx,ly,rx,ry}-{p,n}-tuning   per-axis scaling (100 = unity)
